  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>MAT322 - Composite Simpson's Rule</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Approximate the integral \(\int_{@a@}^{@b@} {@f@} \, dx\) using the Composite Simpson's Rule with \(n = {@n@}\) subintervals.</p>
<p>Give your answer to at least 5 decimal places.</p>
<p>Answer: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>We have \(a={@a@}, b={@b@}, n={@n@}\). The step size is \(h = \frac{b-a}{n} = \frac{{@b-a@}}{{@n@}} = {@h@}\).</p>
<p>The nodes are \(x_j = a + jh\).</p>
<p>Simpson's Rule formula:</p>
<p>\[ S_n = \frac{h}{3} \left[ f(x_0) + 2\sum_{j=1}^{n/2-1} f(x_{2j}) + 4\sum_{j=1}^{n/2} f(x_{2j-1}) + f(x_n) \right] \]</p>
<p>Calculating the terms:</p>
<p>\[ S_{@n@} \approx {@ta1@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>a:0;
b:rand(3)+2;    /* b from 2 to 4 */
n:2*(rand(2)+2); /* n is 4 or 6 */
k:rand(3)+1;
f:exp(k*x);
h:(b-a)/n;
/* Maxima list of nodes */
xs: makelist(a+i*h, i, 0, n);
/* Function values */
ys: map(lambda([x], exp(k*x)), xs);
/* Simpson sum: y0 + yn + 4*sum(odd) + 2*sum(even) */
S: ys[1] + ys[n+1] + 4*sum(ys[2*j], j, 1, n/2) + 2*sum(ys[2*j+1], j, 1, n/2-1);
ta1: float((h/3) * S);
</text>
    </questionvariables>
