<!-- question: 169572 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>MAT322 - Trapezoidal Error Bound</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Determine the minimum number of subintervals \(n\) required to approximate \(\int_{0}^{@b@} \sin({@k@}x) \, dx\) with an error of less than \({@eps@}\) using the Composite Trapezoidal Rule.</p>
<p>\(n = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The error bound for the Composite Trapezoidal Rule is \(|E| \le \frac{(b-a)^3}{12n^2} \max |f''(\xi)|\).</p>
<p>Here \(f(x) = \sin({@k@}x)\), so \(f'(x) = {@k@}\cos({@k@}x)\) and \(f''(x) = -{@k^2@}\sin({@k@}x)\).</p>
<p>The maximum value of \(|f''(x)|\) is \({@k^2@}\).</p>
<p>We need \(\frac{({@b@}-0)^3}{12n^2} ({@k^2@}) < {@eps@}\).</p>
<p>\[ \frac{{@b^3*k^2@}}{12n^2} < {@eps@} \implies n^2 > \frac{{@b^3*k^2@}}{12({@eps@})} \]</p>
<p>\[ n > \sqrt{ \frac{{@b^3*k^2@}}{12({@eps@})} } \approx {@val@} \]</p>
<p>Rounding up, we get \(n = {@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>b:rand(2)+1;    /* b is 1 or 2 */
k:rand(3)+2;    /* k from 2 to 4 */
eps:0.0001;
max_f2: k^2;
val: sqrt( (b^3 * max_f2) / (12 * eps) );
ta1: ceiling(val);
</text>
