  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>MAT322 - Composite Midpoint Rule</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Approximate the integral \(\int_{0}^{@b@} \frac{1}{x+@c@} \, dx\) using the Composite Midpoint Rule with \(n = {@n@}\) subintervals.</p>
<p>Give your answer to at least 5 decimal places.</p>
<p>Answer: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>We have \(a=0, b={@b@}, n={@n@}\). The step size is \(h = \frac{b-a}{n} = {@h@}\).</p>
<p>The midpoints are \(m_j = a + (j-0.5)h\) for \(j=1 \dots n\).</p>
<p>Midpoint Rule formula:</p>
<p>\[ M_n = h \sum_{j=1}^{n} f(m_j) \]</p>
<p>Calculating the terms:</p>
<p>\[ M_{@n@} \approx {@ta1@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>b:rand(3)+2;    /* b from 2 to 4 */
c:rand(3)+1;    /* c from 1 to 3 */
n:2*(rand(2)+1); /* n is 2 or 4 */
h:b/n;
/* Midpoints: (j-0.5)*h */
ms: makelist((j-0.5)*h, j, 1, n);
ys: map(lambda([x], 1/(x+c)), ms);
M: sum(ys[j], j, 1, n);
ta1: float(h * M);
</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text></text>
    </specificfeedback>
    <questionnote format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Int(1/(x+{@c@}), 0, {@b@}), n={@n@}. Ans: {@ta1@}</p>]]></text>
    </questionnote>
    <questiondescription format="html">
      <text></text>
    </questiondescription>
    <questionsimplify>1</questionsimplify>
    <assumepositive>0</assumepositive>
    <assumereal>0</assumereal>
    <prtcorrect format="html">
